Experiment 10 – K-Means Clustering


Aim:
To implement K-Means clustering for segmenting customer 
data based on spending behaviour.



Procedure:
Import libraries and load the customer dataset.
Select suitable features for clustering.
Apply the Elbow method to find the optimal clusters.
Perform K-Means clustering and visualize the results.


Program 10 :


import pandas as pd
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
from sklearn.cluster import KMeans

df = pd.read_csv('Wholesale customers data.csv')

X = df[['Milk','Grocery']]

wcss = []
for i in range(1,11):
    model = KMeans(n_clusters=i,random_state=42,n_init=10)
    model.fit(X)
    wcss.append(model.inertia_)

plt.plot(range(1,11),wcss,marker='o')
plt.show()

model = KMeans(n_clusters=5,random_state=42,n_init=10)
y = model.fit_predict(X)

plt.scatter(X['Milk'],X['Grocery'],c=y)
plt.scatter(model.cluster_centers_[:,0],
            model.cluster_centers_[:,1],marker='X')
plt.show()



Result:
Thus, the K-Means clustering algorithm was successfully implemented 
to segment customers into different groups.

